        "bodySignals": ["A thoughtful, contemplative gaze.","A soft, knowing smile.","Slight nod of the head in acknowledgement.","Calm, steady demeanor.","A feeling of respect or admiration."],
        "otherAttributes": "Cognitive: Involves an intellectual and emotional understanding of worth. | Distinction from Grateful: Grateful is more about receiving kindness; appreciative is about recognizing worth, which can lead to gratitude. | Impact: Enhances engagement with the world and a deeper understanding of quality. | Dealing with it: Spend time reflecting on the qualities you appreciate. Verbalize your appreciation to others. Seek out things that inspire appreciation."
